      "role": "user",
      "content": "The \"latter\" approach sounds a bit risky for us. Our budget for professional cataloging staff is limited, so we'll likely have junior assistants doing much of the heavy lifting. I want to avoid a situation where the archive feels like a lawless, chaotic void where things just vanish into the stacks. Is there anything else we should consider regarding the long-term maintenance of order when dealing with such fragmented, \"rebellious\" materials that refuse to follow the rules of the classification system?",
